'''Shota Yamada''' (山田 翔太, ''Yamada Shōta'', born 21 December 1994) is a Japanese [[field hockey]] player. He competed in the [[2020 Summer Olympics]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://olympics.com/tokyo-2020/olympic-games/en/results/hockey/athlete-profile-n1316842-yamada-shota.htm|title=Hockey YAMADA Shota|work=Tokyo 2020 Olympics|publisher=[[Tokyo Organising Committee of the Olympic and Paralympic Games]]|access-date=2021-07-25|archive-date=2021-07-25|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210725144704/https://olympics.com/tokyo-2020/olympic-games/en/results/hockey/athlete-profile-n1316842-yamada-shota.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref>

He was a part of the Japan squad which won their first [[Asian Games]] gold medal in men's hockey in [[Field hockey at the 2018 Asian Games|2018]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Japan |url=https://tms.fih.ch/teams/4604#players |website=tms.fih.ch |publisher=International Hockey Federation |accessdate=25 November 2018}}</ref>

